<title>UK: EU Santer sees answer to UK quota-hopping demands.</title>
<headline>EU Santer sees answer to UK quota-hopping demands.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer said on Tuesday he was confident of striking a deal at the European Union's Amsterdam summit to end a fisheries row with Britain over so-called quota-hopping.</p>
<p>&quot;I am confident that we will have a solution at the end of the day,&quot; Santer told BBC radio in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>Britain has been angered by EU rules allowing owners of trawlers from other EU countries to buy up the rights to catch fish that under EU quotas was assigned to British fishermen.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
